This would involve creating additional data structures and functions to handle congestion metrics, such as packet loss rate, average latency, and queue length, as well as functions for setting user-defined policies based on the collected metrics. You can use heuristics or machine learning algorithms to make intelligent decisions regarding priority assignments under varying network conditions.

6. Finally, provide APIs for integrating the library with existing network management systems:

Define functions such as `netif_list_get()` to retrieve the dynamic list of interface configurations and `set_policy()` to set user-defined policies based on the collected metrics. Additionally, consider implementing event-based notifications or callback functions for real-time updates to ensure seamless integration with existing network management systems.

