This implementation uses a dynamic list (std::list) to store the PCI_DEVICE_STATUS_RECORD structures, with a circular buffer (boost::container::circular_buffer) as an optimization for efficient resizing. The addDevice() function safely adds new devices and maintains a capacity of 5000 elements in the deviceBuffer.

The getDeviceStatus() function locks the mutex before returning a snapshot of the device list, ensuring thread safety during read operations.

For real-time monitoring, you can wrap the io_service object with a boost::asio::deadline_timer and periodically invoke the getDeviceStatus() method to update devices in the buffer. You can use boost::thread for creating threads and handling concurrent access to the DeviceMonitor instance."]

